{
  "comment": "The vectors pinning what model/chat@1 lets a caller set per brain (Prima.Model): the options describe declares, a chat request's session and options, and a chat response's session. option_kinds are the kinds an option may be. valid_describes are describe answers whose options read as they are (absent reads as none); invalid_describes are refused naming member, the first member that breaks the option shape (options[i] for the entry, options[i].<member> for one of its members, an unknown member by its own name). valid_chat_requests and invalid_chat_requests are requests checked against declared, the options a describe declared; a request's other members are the catalyst's to read and are not checked here. valid_chat_responses are chat answers, a response's data or a refusal's error object, and answer session (null for none); invalid_chat_responses are refused naming member. Read by apps/prima/test/prima/model_test.exs; a model catalyst's own tests read the same file.",
  "option_kinds": ["enum", "string", "integer", "boolean"],
  "valid_describes": [
    {
      "why": "no options member declares none",
      "describe": {"contracts": ["model/chat@1"], "provider": "p", "streaming": true},
      "options": []
    },
    {
      "why": "an empty list declares none",
      "describe": {"provider": "p", "options": []},
      "options": []
    },
